# What Vercel uploads. This changes NOTHING about the folder structure — it only keeps
# non-runtime files out of the deployment. Everything the lesson actually fetches at runtime
# (3_CURRENT_BUILD/HI02H11_L02_S01.html + assets/Audio, assets/Images, assets/UI) is kept.

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Already git-ignored and never committed, but a `vercel` CLI deploy uploads the working
# directory rather than the git tree — so exclude it here too.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# ── Authoring material, not runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────
1_SPEC/
2_MOCKUPS/
5_CURRENT_BUILD_SCREENSHOTS/
*.pptx

# The engine template + its backups. The built HTML is self-contained (the engine is inlined),
# so none of this is fetched by the page.
4_ENGINE/

# ── Build / review by-products inside the bundle ──────────────────────────────
3_CURRENT_BUILD/_review_shots/
3_CURRENT_BUILD/_diagnostics/
3_CURRENT_BUILD/_build_report.json
3_CURRENT_BUILD/*.py
3_CURRENT_BUILD/card.json

# The source GIF. It is re-encoded into assets/UI/train_cover.webp, which is what the page loads.
3_CURRENT_BUILD/assets/GIFandVIDEO/
# Source art the page never requests. train_spritesheet.png is encoded at build time into
# assets/UI/train_spritesheet.webp (5702KB -> 1076KB); train.png is the hi-res standing train,
# now unused because the sheet serves the stopped train too. Kept on disk, kept out of the bundle.
3_CURRENT_BUILD/assets/Images/train_spritesheet.png
3_CURRENT_BUILD/assets/Images/train.png

# ── General ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.orig
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
